        <h2 class="subhead1" id="isPasted" style="text-align: center;">2026 Election &amp; Town Meeting Schedule</h2><h2 style="margin-left: 220px; text-align: center;" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" role="presentation"><br></h2><table><thead><tr><th style="width: 16.4706%;">Date</th><th style="width: 21.7647%;">Election/Town Meeting</th><th style="width: 22.2079%;">Time</th><th style="width: 19.5043%;">Voter Registration Deadline</th><th style="width: 19.6547%;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/12781" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/12781" data-url-hash="7e2dc5573cd823656bc0333416e11d9791dc6de1fee4b88331dcd50c984c0af7" data-url-status="disabled">Vote by Mail Application Deadline</a></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="width: 16.4706%;">Tues, April 7, 2026</td><td style="width: 21.7647%;"><a href="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/13074/2026-Town-Election-Sample-Ballot" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/13074" data-url-hash="1c38843bb664a42c75e3dc9fa0cb11421ae9480a9bf6c267ce0ab77e1d39dd4c" data-url-status="disabled">Annual Town Election</a></td><td style="width: 22.2079%;">polls open<br>7am to 8pm</td><td style="width: 19.5043%;">Sat, March 28, 2026</td><td style="width: 19.6547%;">Tues, March 31, 2026 at 5pm</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 16.4706%;">Mon, May 11, 2026</td><td style="width: 21.7647%;">Annual Town Meeting</td><td style="width: 22.2079%;">begins at 7pm</td><td style="width: 19.5043%;">Fri, May 1, 2026</td><td style="width: 19.6547%; background-color: rgb(0, 0, 0);"><br></td></tr><tr><td style="width: 16.4706%;">Tues, Sept 1, 2026</td><td style="width: 21.7647%;">State Primary<br><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/13566" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Democrat</a><br>​<a href="/DocumentCenter/View/13567" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Republican</a>​​​<br></td><td style="width: 22.2079%;">polls open &nbsp; &nbsp;7am to 8pm</td><td style="width: 19.5043%;">Sat, Aug 22, 2026</td><td style="width: 19.6547%; background-color: rgb(239, 239, 239);">Tues, Aug 25, 2026 at 5pm</td></tr><tr><td style="width: 16.4706%;">Tues, Nov 3, 2026</td><td style="width: 21.7647%;"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/13710" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">State Election</a></td><td style="width: 22.2079%;">polls open &nbsp; 7am to 8pm</td><td style="width: 19.5043%;">Sat, Oct 24, 2026</td><td style="width: 19.6547%; background-color: rgb(239, 239, 239);">Tues, Oct 27, 2026 at 5pm</td></tr></tbody></table><p><br></p><p><img src="/ImageRepository/Document?documentId=13843" class="fr-fil fr-dib" alt="Early Voting Novemnber "></p><h3 id="isPasted">Accessible Voting Equipment</h3><p><span id="isPasted" style='color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: "Open Sans"; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;'>Every early voting and polling location will have one accessible voting machine. &nbsp;The AutoMARK Voter Assist Terminal can assist visually impaired voters.&nbsp;</span> It displays the ballot in high-contrast, magnified text and uses audio cues. The AutoMARK can also read you your ballot before you print it out and submit it.</p><p><a href="https://essvote-1.wistia.com/medias/owccwvkg03" style="box-sizing: border-box; background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 238); text-decoration: none;" target="new" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Watch this AutoMARK Video</a><img data-fr-image-pasted="true" src="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/assets/img/offsite-blackarrow.png" alt="" style="box-sizing: border-box; border-style: none; max-width: 100%;" class="fr-fic fr-dii"> <span id="isPasted" style='color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: "Open Sans"; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;'>for more information on the AutoMARK Voter Assist Terminal</span>.</p><p id="isPasted">&nbsp;___________________________________________________<strong>________________________________________________________________&nbsp;</strong></p><p>NOTICE: On August 13, 2024 the Canton Select Board voted to approve a change in polling location for voters in Precincts 4 and 5.</p><p>Effective immediately the polling location for voters in Precincts 4 and 5 has been changed to <a data-fr-linked="true" href="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/11297/Polling-location-change-notice" id="isPasted" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/11297" data-url-hash="700a58e00c71f5bc71fb71602298171f647291c1050c5182495354744c25816b" data-url-status="disabled">1860 Washington Street</a>, the former site of St. Gerard&apos;s Church.</p><h3 class="subhead2" aria-level="2" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" role="heading"><br></h3><p><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Polling locations are as follows:</strong></span></p><p><strong>Precincts 1 and 6 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Canton High School, 900 Washington St.</strong></p><p><strong>Precincts 2 and 7 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Canton Senior Center, 500 Pleasant St.</strong></p><p><strong>Precinct 3 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Blue Hills Regional School, 800 Randolph St.</strong></p><p><strong>Precincts 4 and 5 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;1860 Washington St. (former site of St. Gerard&apos;s Church)</strong></p><p><br></p><h2 class="subhead1" style="text-align: center;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Elections and Voting</strong></span></h2><p><br></p><p style="text-align: center;"><a aria-label="2022 Vote By Mail Application Opens in new window" href="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/12781/2026-Vote-By-Mail-Application" id="isPasted" rel="noopener" target="_blank" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/DocumentCenter/View/12781" data-url-hash="7e2dc5573cd823656bc0333416e11d9791dc6de1fee4b88331dcd50c984c0af7" data-url-status="disabled"><strong>2026 Vote By Mail Application</strong></a><strong><br></strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong><a aria-label="Register to Vote Online Opens in new window" href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/OVR/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Register to Vote Online</a></strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong><a aria-label="Find My Voter Registration Status Opens in new window" href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/VoterRegistrationSearch/MyVoterRegStatus.aspx" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Find My Voter Registration Status</a></strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><a aria-label="Find my Polling Location Opens in new window" href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/WhereDoIVoteMA/WhereDoIVote" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><strong>Find my Polling Location</strong></a></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong><a aria-label="Track My Ballot Opens in new window" href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/WhereDoIVoteMA/TrackMyBallot" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Track My Ballot</a></strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://www.town.canton.ma.us/988/Citizens-Guide---Town-of-Canton" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message"><strong>Citizen&apos;s Guide - Town of Canton</strong></a></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong><a href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/cis/download/Guide_to_Town_Meetings.pdf" id="isPasted" rel="noopener" target="_blank" aria-label="Citizen's Guide to Town Meetings Opens in new window" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/cis/download/Guide_to_Town_Meetings.pdf" data-url-hash="0fc2fbd7ab665c1fcc4cfc028244b8148e408de0ac448840615f015676f25b4c" data-url-status="disabled">Citizen&apos;s Guide to Town Meetings</a></strong></p><p style="text-align: center;">_______________________________________________________________________________</p><h2 class="subhead1">Public Records Officer</h2><ul><li>Administers and records all oaths of office</li><li>Maintains General By-Laws</li><li>Posts meetings of all governmental bodies</li><li>Provides access to public records</li><li>Responsible for submission of new by-laws to the Office of the Attorney General for approval</li></ul><h2 class="subhead1">Recording Officer</h2><ul><li>Certifies notes for borrowing</li><li>Records all-pole locations approved by the <span style='color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: "Open Sans"; font-size: 14px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: left; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;'>Select</span> Board</li><li>Records and certifies all official action of the town, including Town Meeting legislation and appropriations, Planning and Zoning Board decisions</li><li>Records state tax liens and child support enforcement liens</li></ul><h2 class="subhead1">Vital Records</h2><ul><li>Provides certified copies of vital records and assists with genealogical research</li><li>Registers all vital events (birth, death, and marriages) occurring within the community and those events occurring elsewhere to Canton residents</li></ul><h2 class="subhead1">Voter Registration &amp; Chief Election Official</h2><ul><li>Assists voters interested in running for public office</li><li>Conducts all town, state and federal elections and certifies nomination papers and initiative petitions</li><li>Conducts annual census, annual street lists and assists the Jury Commissioner with the preparation with the Jury List</li><li>Supervises voter registration and absentee balloting</li></ul>
    </div>

